ref_solution:
We have the equation $\frac{2x-1}{2x+2}=\frac{x-3}{x-1}$. Cross-multiplying and simplifying, we get \begin{align*}
(2x-1)(x-1)&=(2x+2)(x-3)\\
2x^2 - x - 2x + 1 &= 2x^2 + 2x - 3 \cdot 2x - 3 \cdot 2 \\
2x^2 - 3x + 1&=2x^2-4x-6\\
x&=\boxed{-7}
\end{align*}

Isolating $g(x),$ we find: \begin{align*}
g(x) &= (x + 1) - (8x^4-7x^2 + 8x - 7) \\
&= x + 1 - 8x^4 + 7x^2 - 8x + 7 \\
&= \boxed{-8 x^4+7x^2-7x+8}.
\end{align*}

